1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,556
Hi, I'm Shivam Gupta.

2
00:00:02,556 --> 00:00:07,242
This is Runway Guard, a tool that asks whether your
crypto treasury

3
00:00:07,242 --> 00:00:08,920
can still pay your team.

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:12,897
A portfolio balance tells you what your assets are
worth today.

5
00:00:12,897 --> 00:00:17,291
It does not tell you whether the next payroll payment
is covered

6
00:00:17,291 --> 00:00:20,312
if prices fall or funds become inaccessible.

7
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:22,755
Here is a fictional sample team.

8
00:00:22,755 --> 00:00:28,189
It has crypto holdings, twenty-five thousand dollars in
fiat cash, and forty-two

9
00:00:28,189 --> 00:00:31,178
thousand dollars in monthly operating costs.

10
00:00:31,178 --> 00:00:37,140
I can enter balances manually or import a CSV, then
schedule payroll

11
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:39,332
and add one-off expenses.

12
00:00:39,332 --> 00:00:43,607
Refreshing fetches real CoinMarketCap quotes.

13
00:00:43,607 --> 00:00:49,048
The evidence view shows the response and timestamps
behind the calculation.

14
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:54,213
Now I apply a forty percent decline to volatile assets
and a

15
00:00:54,213 --> 00:00:56,193
ten percent USDC depeg.

16
00:00:56,193 --> 00:00:59,332
These are assumptions, not predictions.

17
00:00:59,332 --> 00:01:04,403
The chart compares current and stressed coverage as
expenses come due.

18
00:01:04,403 --> 00:01:07,713
Locked assets cannot fund those expenses.

19
00:01:07,713 --> 00:01:12,528
A recurring payroll row schedules its share of monthly
burn.

20
00:01:12,528 --> 00:01:15,511
The app does not count that expense twice.

21
00:01:15,511 --> 00:01:19,732
I can also simulate losing access to an asset and see
how

22
00:01:19,732 --> 00:01:21,732
the available funds change.

23
00:01:21,732 --> 00:01:26,217
The reserve what-if estimates how much fiat we need for
our chosen

24
00:01:26,217 --> 00:01:31,518
reserve period, and which available volatile holdings
could fill the gap under

25
00:01:31,518 --> 00:01:32,741
these assumptions.

26
00:01:32,741 --> 00:01:34,474
This is a planning estimate.

27
00:01:34,474 --> 00:01:39,891
The app does not execute trades, and reported market
volume does not

28
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:41,803
guarantee sale proceeds.

29
00:01:41,803 --> 00:01:47,039
A saved report preserves the inputs, quotes and
assumptions so someone else

30
00:01:47,039 --> 00:01:49,971
can review the result after prices change.

31
00:01:49,971 --> 00:01:55,681
The commercial hypothesis is a focused tool for small
crypto-native teams.

32
00:01:55,681 --> 00:02:00,891
The next step is to validate a weekly planning workflow
with those

33
00:02:00,891 --> 00:02:04,048
teams, then add paid reviews and alerts.

34
00:02:04,048 --> 00:02:08,943
Runway Guard connects a changing market to a concrete
question: can we

35
00:02:08,943 --> 00:02:11,250
cover the obligations coming due?
